CImg changes
============

This file lists changes that have been done to the CImg header file in this
project. Some of these might have been upstreamed or not, or upstream might
have changed them in some newer release.

Changes are listed newest first.

30/09/2026
----------

* CImg::get_warp(): removed the OpenMP "parallel for" pragma from the six
  forward-warp paths (mode 2 and mode 3, for 1D/2D/3D warping fields, with
  linear or higher interpolation).

  A forward warp scatters source pixels into the result through
  set_linear_atX{Y,Z}(), which accumulates with an iterated read-modify-write
  blend:

      dest = (T)(w1*value + w2*dest)

  When several source pixels map to the same destination, threads running the
  loop concurrently read and write that same cell, so the accumulated value
  depends on the order in which the scatters happen to interleave. The result
  was therefore non-deterministic and, for maps that contract, visibly wrong:
  on a 200x150 test image roughly 2300 of 30000 pixels differed from the
  serial result, with an average difference of about 0.27 (compared with pixel
  values of order 1). Atomic updates would not fix this, because the operation
  is not a commutative reduction - the order of the blends changes the answer -
  so only a fixed scatter order is correct.

  Marked in the header with "[imager] Kept serial" comments. Note that upstream
  CImg 4.06 still contains the same bug, so re-vendoring a newer CImg.h will
  reintroduce it; tests/testthat/test_warp_determinism.R guards against that.

  The backward-warp paths (mode 0 and mode 1) were left parallelised: they
  gather into disjoint output cells and are unaffected.

11/05/2024
----------

* Increase buffer used for sprintf output, caught by gcc 14.
* Avoid referring to null stdout, caught by gcc 14.
* Avoid potential null dereferences, caught by gcc 13 and 14.

